      "math_academy_id": "q-71761",
      "knowledge_point_id": "90033e91-fdb2-5aa0-8cce-76762a38ffd2",
      "knowledge_point": "Integrating Using Arcsine",
      "problem": "$\\int (8x-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}})\\text{d}x=$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that \n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x+C.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (8x-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}})\\text{d}x & =\\int 8x\\,\\text{d}x-\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =8\\int x\\,\\text{d}x-\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4{x}^{2}-\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
